1
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:06,820
This is Trigun.

2
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:33,820
guitar solo

3
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:38,677
The Typhoon is currently
gaining strength and will be

4
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:41,777
passing approximately 30
miles away from New Oregon.

5
00:01:41,860 --> 00:01:44,137
The gale is expected
to last until morning.

6
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:48,337
Please be advised that high wind warnings
are still in effect until further night.

7
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,840
So this is a Typhoon.

8
00:01:50,280 --> 00:01:52,037
I've heard that one can be strong,

9
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:55,077
but I never dreamed it could
blow with this kind of force.

10
00:01:55,160 --> 00:01:56,217
Yeah, you're right.

11
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:59,057
In fact, this one is so huffy,
she must be related to...

12
00:01:59,140 --> 00:02:00,340
Mr. Vash!

13
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:03,080
Her name is Jacqueline, and...

14
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:07,870
Mr.

15
00:02:07,953 --> 00:02:09,797
Vash, excuse me, but
may we have a moment...

16
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:11,300
to speak with you?

17
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:20,120
Please don't look for me, Vash.

18
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:22,060
Damn, he got us!

19
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:25,637
Either he's incredibly slippery, or he's
just gone completely out of his mind!

20
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:27,817
I can't believe he'd actually
go out in these conditions!

21
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:29,840
No problem, we'll find it. Huh?

22
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:34,757
I suspected he might try this, so when I
brought him breakfast earlier this morning,

23
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:37,677
I slipped one of these
into the food on his plate.

24
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,700
Oh, my gosh.

25
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,157
That's a transmitting device.

26
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:42,917
I'm amazed the company let
you have something like that.

27
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:46,117
Since I'm always messing up, the chief
gave it to me as a going-away present.

28
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:48,847
He says it'll keep anyone
from outwitting me.

29
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:52,688
Millie, I hate to tell you, but
that's nothing to brag about.

30
00:02:54,700 --> 00:02:56,680
Look, look, he's really close by.

31
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:59,429
We're catching up already!

32
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:03,200
Yeah! Warmer! Warmer! Warmer!

33
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:08,760
Oh my god!

34
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:11,400
He changed into a cat this time! Millie!

35
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,310
Vash.

36
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:36,030
Vash!

37
00:03:38,320 --> 00:03:39,400
Come on, Vash.

38
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:40,620
Stand up already.

39
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:42,890
Let's go!

40
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:45,670
Hey!

41
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:47,560
Don't be that way.

42
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:49,257
It's just you and me here.

43
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:51,928
We should at least try
to act like brothers.

44
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:57,670
Murderer!

45
00:03:57,940 --> 00:03:59,457
Your whole life is a lie!

46
00:03:59,540 --> 00:04:01,777
You killed Rem! The crew!

47
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:03,200
You killed them all!

48
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,940
Yeah, spectacular, huh?

49
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:09,540
They all die.

50
00:04:09,980 --> 00:04:10,897
Except, of course,

51
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:15,098
for the fraction who will survive
because of Rem's incessant meddling.

52
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,310
Knives?

53
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:19,450
You...

54
00:04:19,533 --> 00:04:21,060
You aren't even human!

55
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:23,700
Damn straight I'm not!

56
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:27,320
How dare you call me
those damn perfect things!

57
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:28,900
How dare you!

58
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:31,040
Never compare me to that!

59
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:36,200
You're nothing but garbage.

60
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:38,920
I will kill you all.

61
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:42,300
Only we will be left on this planet.

62
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:44,970
Rem!

63
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:47,540
Now, Bash, take care of Noss!

64
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:56,945
I know what I have to do, Rem.

65
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,772
I can't wait any longer.

66
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,194
It's time to face him.

67
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:01,600
I have to be ready.

68
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:06,777
Jacqueline's ankle should
pass near the Craggy Bluff,

69
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:10,060
blowing to the southeast
at exactly 1.22 p .m.

70
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:12,185
I'm counting on you, old chum.

71
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:19,688
If you're wrong about this, you crazy
old geezer, I'll haunt you to the grave!

72
00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:32,117
I still feel like I'm having a freaking
heart attack every time I do this!

73
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,157
This thing's going ba-da-boom ba-da-boom!

74
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:36,475
I thought you were committing suicide!

75
00:05:36,760 --> 00:05:37,590
Suicide?

76
00:05:37,673 --> 00:05:39,797
I strongly disapprove of
suicide, it's just a...

77
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:40,710
huh?

78
00:05:41,940 --> 00:05:42,770
Wolfwood?

79
00:05:42,853 --> 00:05:43,972
What are you doing here?

80
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:47,137
First you're crying your eyes
out like an abandoned baby,

81
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:49,277
and then you're running
around jumping off cliffs.

82
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,889
What the hell's the
matter with you anyway?

83
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:52,960
I'm visiting.

84
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:55,180
Say what?

85
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:57,160
I'm visiting the folks.

86
00:05:57,560 --> 00:06:00,057
Yeah, right. What do they have?

87
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:01,477
A summer cottage in the sky?

88
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:03,736
I'm really getting sick of your lies.

89
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:08,910
Huh?

90
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:10,329
Hey, what the hell's that?

91
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:11,832
Just what it looks like.

92
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:15,100
It's a ship that didn't
quite crash 130 years ago.

93
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:16,980
This is unbelievable.

94
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:22,195
Who'd have known that the lost
technology was still preserved like this?

95
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:25,987
Wait, did you say you're
visiting your folks?

96
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:28,937
Does that mean people are
actually living up here?

97
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:33,314
I think that you'll be their first
house guest to visit in over 20 years.

98
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,750
Mr.

99
00:06:48,833 --> 00:06:51,517
Legato, it has happened as expected.

100
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:53,600
He has made his move.

101
00:06:55,780 --> 00:07:00,420
Also, the last stampede appears to
be working with the Minister Clan.

102
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:05,097
I suspect this man is...

103
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:06,120
Never mind him.

104
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:09,340
Your task will remain the
same no matter who he is.

105
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:11,900
Yes, Master.

106
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,900
You're such a fool.

107
00:07:16,400 --> 00:07:19,576
Had you behaved, you might
have lived to see Doomsday.

108
00:07:19,820 --> 00:07:22,360
But I must say, I am pleased.

109
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:27,315
For now, I have an opportunity to
fulfill another of my master's wishes.

110
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:39,237
Doctor, you won't believe this,

111
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:43,026
are you going to tell me that
someone is here from the outside?

112
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:46,337
Oh, yeah, it's been a
long time, but he's back.

113
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:49,817
So, Brad, have you ever met him before?

114
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:53,217
Well, yeah, I have, but I
was just a kid back then.

115
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:56,317
This will be the first time
you've met a real legend.

116
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,957
He's changed over the years.

117
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,020
Come with me.

118
00:08:02,180 --> 00:08:05,180
So he really is back, what do you know?

119
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:10,504
Amazing how many years has it been
since I last opened this door?

120
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:21,700
Is he there is that him?

121
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:27,230
What do you mean?

122
00:08:27,313 --> 00:08:28,617
You're telling me now I can't come in?

123
00:08:28,700 --> 00:08:31,097
Who do you think you are,
you needle-logging idiot?

124
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:32,010
Ow!

125
00:08:32,093 --> 00:08:32,923
Oh, hey, Doc.

126
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:35,049
Is that your great legend?

127
00:08:35,400 --> 00:08:36,880
Is that rule him, huh?

128
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:38,460
What a relief.

129
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:40,151
He hasn't changed at all.

130
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,997
Your name's Brad, isn't it?

131
00:08:48,080 --> 00:08:49,551
Man, you sure got taller.

132
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:51,170
Yeah, right.

133
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:52,535
By the way, who's he?

134
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:56,117
You know, to tell you the
truth, I'm not really sure.

135
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,030
Look,

136
00:08:57,113 --> 00:09:00,557
I don't mind you wandering around the
place, but outsiders are not welcome here.

137
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:02,699
Oh, then I'll be like that big guy.

138
00:09:03,740 --> 00:09:04,570
Okay.

139
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:13,240
Don't stare. Come on inside.

140
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:17,020
Get used to it. You win. I'll behave.

141
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:18,710
Huh? Huh?

142
00:09:18,793 --> 00:09:19,623
Huh?

143
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:29,970
Fast!

144
00:09:30,053 --> 00:09:30,883
Oh!

145
00:09:30,966 --> 00:09:32,837
Gee, this is all rather
sudden, young lady.

146
00:09:32,920 --> 00:09:37,685
I may have a reputation of being easy,
but even I need a bit of advanced warning.

147
00:09:42,080 --> 00:09:44,420
Jessica! That's right! Wow!

148
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:46,117
I can't believe you remembered me!

149
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:48,620
This is the best date ever!

150
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:53,977
Well, Vash, this must
be your girlfriend, huh?

151
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:55,660
You are one lucky devil.

152
00:09:57,840 --> 00:09:58,877
What's the matter?

153
00:09:58,960 --> 00:10:00,220
Did I embarrass you?

154
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:07,077
Sorry, but I have to speak with
the doctor for a little while.

155
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:07,990
Hey!

156
00:10:08,073 --> 00:10:09,480
Now that's not fair! Jessica!

157
00:10:11,500 --> 00:10:12,912
Come see me after, okay?

158
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,040
Like right after?

159
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:15,808
I'll hate you if you don't.

160
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,240
OK, all right.

161
00:10:18,040 --> 00:10:19,511
I'll be back in a minute.

162
00:10:20,280 --> 00:10:22,640
So, Vash, how's Max? Is he well?

163
00:10:22,840 --> 00:10:24,337
Oh, yeah, he's doing great.

164
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:26,857
He has staring contests
with forecast charts.

165
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:27,770
Huh?

166
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:31,457
Hmm, well, now, I haven't
introduced myself.

167
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:32,716
My name is Wolf Wa -

168
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:35,380
Can you blame her?

169
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:37,177
The people who live on
this ship aren't about

170
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:39,277
to trust a bunch of
outsiders bringing in war?

171
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:40,190
and violence.

172
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:43,260
You make this place stink like gunpowder.

173
00:10:43,840 --> 00:10:45,377
Stay put until he gets back.

174
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:47,720
I don't want any trouble. Got that?

175
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:53,562
You could at least offer
me a drink or something.

176
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:58,257
For crying out loud, I am not the
least bit happy about this Millie.

177
00:10:58,340 --> 00:10:59,497
We have just found him again,

178
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:01,517
and then we let him slip right
out from under our noses.

179
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:03,597
I know all that, but
we can't go out there.

180
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:04,777
It's too dangerous.

181
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:07,860
We have to, and besides,
danger is part of the job.

182
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:51,200
An entire city is surrounded
by lost technology.

183
00:11:52,140 --> 00:11:55,258
I'm saying it to you little
by little, needle noggin.

184
00:11:58,420 --> 00:11:59,832
Get out of here, mister!

185
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:02,640
I'm so sorry, but he's right.

186
00:12:03,940 --> 00:12:06,417
I hate to say it, but I
feel the same way he does.

187
00:12:06,500 --> 00:12:08,437
I'm begging you for the good of all of us.

188
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:09,932
Please leave this place.

189
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:16,837
Why, so you can all just carry on with
your perfect cozy little shuffle of lives?

190
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:17,750
Huh?

191
00:12:17,833 --> 00:12:20,237
You need to realize your
plants are not inexhaustible.

192
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:22,849
They could very easily
break down some day.

193
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,677
You can't cling on to them forever.

194
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:26,797
This technology has a finite lifespan.

195
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:27,957
What are you telling us?

196
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:30,817
You have no idea how hard it
is to maintain these systems.

197
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:33,677
We're not planning on anything
shutting down for a long time now.

198
00:12:33,760 --> 00:12:35,497
And anything's better
than living out there.

199
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:37,637
I've heard that people's
lives are meaningless to you,

200
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,737
so why should we listen to
anything you have to say?

201
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:40,938
Yeah, that's right!

202
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:46,115
No matter what you say, it's
not gonna change anything.

203
00:12:46,380 --> 00:12:48,617
You better get used to
the idea that someday

204
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:51,288
you're gonna all live
on that desert planet.

205
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:55,937
Anything new happen while I was away?

206
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:57,280
No, not much.

207
00:12:57,500 --> 00:13:00,157
They're still sleeping
in suspended animation.

208
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,070
Really?

209
00:13:01,153 --> 00:13:02,780
We were all worried sick.

210
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:06,065
You've been out of touch
for nearly five years.

211
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:07,320
I'm sorry.

212
00:13:08,020 --> 00:13:08,850
Sure.

213
00:13:08,933 --> 00:13:09,763
Like you even care.

214
00:13:09,846 --> 00:13:13,417
Five years is probably nothing more
than the blink of an eye for you anyway.

215
00:13:13,500 --> 00:13:14,330
That's enough, Brad.

216
00:13:14,413 --> 00:13:16,062
Vash is not that kind of person.

217
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:18,470
Person?

218
00:13:18,553 --> 00:13:19,580
You gotta be kidding.

219
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:24,540
Since you have returned, I suppose
that means it's not over yet.

220
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:29,082
Did you come into contact with him
during the fifth moon incident?

221
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:32,917
Not directly, but my guess would be
that he had something to do with it.

222
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:37,577
I have absolutely no memory of it happening,
just like the time before in July.

223
00:13:37,660 --> 00:13:38,520
Tell me, Vash.

224
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:40,040
Did you fire it?

225
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:43,280
Hey, Mr. Legend!

226
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:45,957
Since you're the one that
fired off the big weapon,

227
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:47,557
doesn't that make you more
destructive than knives?

228
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:48,816
I said enough, Brad!

229
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:50,720
Well, doesn't it? Brad!

230
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,370
That's right.

231
00:13:53,453 --> 00:13:54,419
I suppose it does.

232
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:55,699
That is not funny.

233
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,377
That is not funny!

234
00:13:57,460 --> 00:14:00,177
It's the whole damn world
we're talking about here.

235
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:02,319
Don't you think I am aware of that?

236
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:03,270
However,

237
00:14:03,353 --> 00:14:06,237
the only one who has been able
to oppose knives fight off his

238
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:10,080
demons and survive them is that
gentleman holding by the neck?

239
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:13,780
I'm asking you to please trust me!

240
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:16,710
Please?

241
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:26,460
I'm sorry.

242
00:14:27,480 --> 00:14:28,310
He's right.

243
00:14:28,393 --> 00:14:29,460
I can't blame him.

244
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:33,811
Too simple and ordinary people,
I must seem like a monster.

245
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,780
Well, that's half his problem.

246
00:14:35,980 --> 00:14:40,568
He's hopelessly in love with Jessica,
and he just told her for the first time.

247
00:14:41,640 --> 00:14:42,470
Jessica.

248
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,527
I'm sorry, Brad, but
I'm going to marry back.

249
00:14:47,480 --> 00:14:50,560
I'm getting very fast! Fast! Fast!

250
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,826
Well, that's the other
half of Brad's problem.

251
00:14:54,820 --> 00:14:55,761
What's in there?

252
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:02,053
A little something you might be needing.

253
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:12,338
He hasn't been much fun,
but I'm sure glad he's back.

254
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:14,168
At least he hasn't changed.

255
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:15,760
He hasn't changed a bit.

256
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:17,460
Hey, Matt!

257
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,270
Wait!

258
00:15:19,380 --> 00:15:20,360
Wait for me!

259
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:29,760
Look at me! Look at me! I'm in love!

260
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:38,117
This damn ship is full of nothing
but rotten, ignorant people.

261
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:41,141
Doesn't anyone trust the
word of a priest anymore?

262
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:44,377
Hey, up and up in there!

263
00:15:44,460 --> 00:15:50,580
What's going on what's wrong
what the hell's going on in there

264
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:17,342
I mean, it was exactly
like this when I got here.

265
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:21,500
Hey, listen to me! What happened?

266
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:24,206
Brad, it's Terry and Natasha.

267
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:35,480
It was me, Brad.

268
00:16:40,280 --> 00:16:42,280
I'm asking you to please trust me.

269
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:47,088
There's no way you can
prove your innocence!

270
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:49,000
This is great, Doc.

271
00:16:49,200 --> 00:16:50,737
It's by far the smoothest one yet.

272
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:51,777
I'm glad you like it.

273
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:52,737
Now, we'd better hurry.

274
00:16:52,820 --> 00:16:54,057
It's gotten very late.

275
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:56,081
Jessica will be furious with you.

276
00:16:58,900 --> 00:16:59,730
Strange.

277
00:16:59,813 --> 00:17:01,188
She said she would be here.

278
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,880
Oh, yes, that present.

279
00:17:05,060 --> 00:17:06,657
She wanted to give it to you.

280
00:17:06,740 --> 00:17:10,622
She's been looking forward to your
return for quite some time now.

281
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,120
Doc, what is this?

282
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:24,237
I'll say it one more
time, I didn't kill him.

283
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:27,160
Shut up, you're a killer
and a liar, Outsider!

284
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:30,228
You're serious, aren't you?

285
00:17:30,740 --> 00:17:32,681
You really want to fight me, huh?

286
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:39,632
Hey, what are you doing?

287
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:44,320
Joseph! Move it!

288
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,211
You did this, didn't you?

289
00:17:55,800 --> 00:17:57,080
Back off now, Brad.

290
00:17:57,380 --> 00:18:01,380
You couldn't possibly survive a
fight against this breed of bad guy.

291
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:09,785
The warm-out fight, I presume?

292
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:12,680
Oh, so you know my name.

293
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:14,760
Well, I must say I mind.

294
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:18,179
I'm afraid we've never met,
but I have heard of you.

295
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,809
An interesting reputation.

296
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:24,580
You are the man who rings the black
funeral bell, chapel... Don't say it!

297
00:18:24,720 --> 00:18:26,073
Enough with your butts!

298
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:39,800
This is just a warm-up,
both for him and for me.

299
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:41,997
You are smart, Preacher.

300
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:46,277
It would be easy to destroy you at
this point, but that would be boring.

301
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:49,920
To make the game more
interesting, I've added a sweet L.

302
00:18:50,780 --> 00:18:51,610
Jessica!

303
00:18:52,120 --> 00:18:55,600
I have been watching you through
his eyes the entire time.

304
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:59,497
I know that you have very strong
feelings for this young lady.

305
00:18:59,580 --> 00:19:00,410
Very touching.

306
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:03,480
You do know what I have
in mind, do you not?

307
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:10,136
You pacifistic fool, don't
you realize this is a trap?

308
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:12,820
I know what it is.

309
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,200
Then lower your piece.

310
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,480
I can't.

311
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:19,699
I just don't see any way
out of this damn situation!

312
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:22,660
There is another way.

313
00:19:23,220 --> 00:19:27,455
If we simply ignore the girl's plight,
we'll definitely make it through.

314
00:19:29,220 --> 00:19:30,300
What did you say?

315
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:33,097
I think that's the best
option at this point in time.

316
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:36,277
It's the only logical way any
of us will survive against them.

317
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:37,380
No, you can't!

318
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:38,870
However,

319
00:19:38,953 --> 00:19:41,917
I do know of a guy who whines,
cries, and throws tantrums,

320
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:45,176
and he somehow manages to
find a way to save everyone.

321
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:48,626
He's a crazy man who's
not afraid of anything.

322
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:52,918
Even though he's been scarred from
head to toe, he'll always be there.

323
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:07,170
Jessica!

324
00:20:07,253 --> 00:20:08,083
Jess, are you alright?

325
00:20:08,166 --> 00:20:09,397
They didn't hurt you, did they?

326
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,656
I guess they didn't.

327
00:20:10,860 --> 00:20:12,154
What took you so long?

328
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:28,040
A flower.

329
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:29,340
A red flower.

330
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:30,838
Isn't it beautiful?

331
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:32,905
They call this one a geranium.

332
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:35,397
There are many other
types of flowers on Earth

333
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:37,837
of all different colors
and shapes and sizes.

334
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:40,717
They hold a very special
place in people's hearts.

335
00:20:40,800 --> 00:20:42,271
Can you eat them forever?

336
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,308
Some flowers can be eating.

337
00:20:44,820 --> 00:20:45,996
Do you like flowers?

338
00:20:46,440 --> 00:20:49,100
I love flowers, especially red ones.

339
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:51,418
You know, they can be very symbolic.

340
00:20:51,620 --> 00:20:56,326
Even the tiniest flowers which brave the
elements behold a magnificent strength.

341
00:20:57,520 --> 00:20:58,580
And Vash,

342
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:05,240
in the language of the flower, red geraniums
represent determination and courage.

343
00:21:18,260 --> 00:21:19,400
Hey, wait a sec!

344
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:21,257
Where'd you get the red coat?

345
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:22,520
I don't believe it.

346
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:24,540
It's Vash the Stampede!

347
00:21:29,540 --> 00:21:31,320
Oh, Vash! Vash! Vash!

348
00:21:31,480 --> 00:21:32,680
I'm so scared!

349
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:34,460
Knock it off!

350
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:36,129
Come on, will you stop it?

351
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:37,969
You're not upset, are you?

352
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:41,160
You act like it's all over.

353
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:45,040
But let me assure you, some of
my children are still there.

354
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:51,160
Besides, did you really think that the
gung-ho guns only come to call one at a time?

355
00:21:51,520 --> 00:21:52,696
What are you saying?

356
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:08,940
Three of them.

357
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:11,297
That is correct.

358
00:22:11,380 --> 00:22:13,840
I have sent three demons.

359
00:22:14,180 --> 00:22:18,180
They have arrived and will be
visiting you very soon. Welcome.

360
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:22,500
This is your big comeback
celebration by Ashton Stampede.

361
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:50,380
The blue sky in the middle of
the sky, the wind is the future.

362
00:22:51,980 --> 00:22:55,777
The light of the day of the sky,

363
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:58,937
the light of the day?

364
00:22:59,020 --> 00:23:00,617
Thank

365
00:23:00,700 --> 00:23:07,700
you

366
00:23:26,340 --> 00:23:27,197
so

367
00:23:27,280 --> 00:23:29,000
much for watching.

368
00:23:42,020 --> 00:23:46,537
I'll see you

369
00:23:46,620 --> 00:23:49,400
next time.

370
00:24:07,180 --> 00:24:11,497
There's something you can't give up,
there's something you want to protect.

371
00:24:11,580 --> 00:24:16,051
There's a time you must take a stand,
no matter what kind of pain awaits us.

372
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:20,180
The man clad in the red coat
took up his gun once again,

373
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:22,480
in order to stop the sadness,

374
00:24:23,400 --> 00:24:25,100
in order to stop the hate.

375
00:24:26,140 --> 00:24:30,140
I keep the word of the red geranium,
which I was taught so long ago.

376
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:34,820
I keep the courage and
determination deep in my heart.
